NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000013 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000014 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000015 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000016 "Task::Weaken - Ensure that a platform has weaken support"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000017 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000018 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000019 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000020 "version 1.06"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000021 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 "One recurring problem in modules that use L<Scalar::Util>'s C<weaken>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "function is that it is not present in the pure-perl variant."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "While this isn't necessarily always a problem in a straight CPAN-based"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 "Perl environment, some operating system distributions only include the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "pure-Perl versions, don't include the XS version, and so weaken is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 "then \"missing\" from the platform, B<despite> passing a dependency on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "L<Scalar::Util> successfully."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "Most notably this is RedHat Linux at time of writing, but other come"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "and go and do the same thing, hence \"recurring problem\"."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "The normal solution is to manually write tests in each distribution"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "to ensure that C<weaken> is available."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "This restores the functionality testing to a dependency you do once"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 "in your F<Makefile.PL>, rather than something you have to write extra"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "tests for each time you write a module."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "It should also help make the package auto-generators for the various"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 "operating systems play more nicely, because it introduces a dependency"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "that they B<have> to have a proper weaken in order to work."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "=head2 How this Task works"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "Part of the problem seems to stem from the fact that some distributions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "continue to include modules even if they fail some of their tests."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "To get around that for this module, it will do a few dirty tricks."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 "If L<Scalar::Util> is not available at all, it will issue a normal"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 "dependency on the module. However, if L<Scalar::Util> is relatively"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 "new ( it is E<gt>= 1.19 ) and the module does B<not> have weaken, the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 "install will bail out altogether with a long error encouraging the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 "user to seek support from their vendor (this problem happens most"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 "often in vendor-packaged Perl versions)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 "This distribution also contains tests to ensure that weaken is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 "available using more normal methods."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 "So if your module uses C<weaken>, you can just add the following to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 "your L<Module::Install>-based F<Makefile.PL> (or equivalent)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 "  requires 'Task::Weaken' => 0;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 ""
